WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.120
What is the Council presidency
and how does it work?

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.900
The Council presidency is responsible
for driving forward the Council's work.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.960
Each member state is called upon, in turn,

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.230
to take on this role and ensure continuity

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.830
in the Council's agenda.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.570
The Council presidency has several key tasks:

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.750
It plans and chairs meetings of the ministers

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.420
and working groups of civil servants

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.450
discussing EU legislation in the Council.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.280
But in the case of foreign affairs,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.980
it is the EU's High Representative

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.829
for Foreign and Security Policy

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:37.170
who plans and chairs meetings.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.379
The presidency also represents the Council

00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:40.809
in relations with the Commission

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:43.880
and the European Parliament.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.729
It negotiates on behalf of the Council

00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:47.770
to reach agreement on legislative files

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.010
with the other EU institutions.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.850
The presidency of the Council rotates among

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:56.389
the EU member states every 6 months.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.389
This means that each

00:00:57.389 --> 00:00:58.469
country takes it in turns

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:00.030
to lead the Council and prepare

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.249
a 6-month work programme.

00:01:03.249 --> 00:01:04.960
The order of rotation of the presidencies

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.970
is set by the Council.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.530
Member states holding the presidency

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.070
work together in groups of three, called trios.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.210
They set long-term goals

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.110
and prepare a common agenda of topics

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.580
to be addressed by the Council

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.990
over an 18 month period.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:21.990
These long-term goals

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.200
are guided by the priorities

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.920
adopted by the European Council

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.660
in its strategic agenda,

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:27.860
covering for instance:

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.530
jobs, growth and competitiveness

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.130
energy and climate policies

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.490
freedom, security and justice

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.640
Find out when your country

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.270
will next be leading the Council

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:41.159
and much more on Consilium.europa.eu

